keyUsage.description:
The parameter defines the purpose (e.g., encipherment, signature, certificate signing) of the key contained in the certificate. It is a bit string. When a bit is set to 1, it means the key usage corresponding to the bit applies to the certificate. In RFC5280, the meaning of the bits starting from the left-most is following: 
Bit 0: Digital Signature;
Bit 1: Content Commitment;
Bit 2: Key Encipherment;
Bit 3: DataEncipherment;
Bit 4: Key Agreement;
Bit 5: Key Certificate Sign;
Bit 6: Sign CRL;
Bit 7: Encipher Only; 
Bit 8: Decipher Only;

maxNumCaConfUe.description:
Threshold to limit the maximum number of carrier aggregation configured UEs in a PCell (P-LNCEL); 
UEs may have 1 PCell (P-LNCEL) and 1 or several SCell(s) (S-LNCEL).
Carrier aggregated UEs with 1 or more SCell need more resources than nonCA Ues (PUCCH and MAC PS);
Therefore limiting the amount of CA-UEs is necessary.

In case the threshold is modified online and the value is decreased, existing CA-UEs may stay in the cell, but the new value applies to new admision checks only.

minNumEmergencySessions.description:
Minimum number reserved RRC connection resources for Emergency Sessions. This parameter is only used by AirScale in case dynamic PUCCH features are not activated.

Note: This parameter is even relevant, if emergency call handling is de-activated ( actEmerCallRedir or actIMSEmerSessR9 are set to false) in order to have reserve for high priority calls;

If dynamic PUCCH features are activated and AirScale is deployed, then the aPucchMinNumEmergencySessions parameter has to be configured.

