ttibOperMode.description:
This parameter determines
- which set of threshold conditions is used for entering / leaving TTI Bundling mode
- whether TTI bundling can be started or stopped while the UE is configured with measurement gaps. 
BLER-based thresholds include TTIB mode entry conditions on the MCS assigned to a UE, the maximum number of PRBs that link adaptation has determined, and the current BLER. 
SINR-based thresholds do not depend on link adaptation. They include the UE’s power headroom, so essentially they are based on how much energy the UE can deliver at the eNB’s receiver input.

values:
blerBasedNotWithMeasGap: BLER-based threshold used for TTIB mode switching; 
TTI Bundling not allowed if measurement gaps are configured
blerBasedTtibOnAllowed; BLER-based threshold used for TTIB mode switching; 
entering TTIB mode is allowed with configured measurement gaps
blerBasedTtibOnOffAllowed: BLER-based threshold used for TTIB mode switching; 
entering and leaving TTIB mode is allowed with configured measurement gaps
sinrBasedNotWithMeasGap: SINR-based threshold used for TTIB mode switching; 
TTI Bundling not allowed if measurement gaps are configured
sinrBasedTtibOnAllowed: SINR-based threshold used for TTIB mode switching; 
entering TTIB mode is allowed with configured measurement gaps
sinrBasedTtibOnOffAllowed: SINR-based threshold used for TTIB mode switching; 
entering and leaving TTIB mode is allowed with configured measurement gaps

